      "problem": "Find the value of $\\sqrt[3]{-6}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{-6}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{-6}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we re-write the product using the cube:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[3]{-6}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{-6}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{-6}={(\\sqrt[3]{-6})}^{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we use that  the cube and the cube root cancel each other out. So, we have\n\n$$\n{(\\sqrt[3]{-6})}^{3}=-6.\n$$",
